5. Build Rules for Who Receives Help
A charitable nonprofit cannot simply give funds to whichever individual someone personally chooses. Assistance should serve a genuine charitable class—such as low-income students in a defined area or financially vulnerable patients referred by a partner—and recipients should be chosen through objective, documented need-based criteria. 
