8. A Strong First-Year Strategy
For the first year, I recommend:

Select one community or geographic area.

Select one group of beneficiaries.

Select one core program.

Establish one or two trusted partners.

Set a fixed annual assistance budget.

Develop written eligibility rules.

Pay vendors or service providers directly when practical.

Track each dollar and each outcome.

Publish a simple annual impact report.

Expand only after the pilot is working reliably.

Example first-year target:

Support 50 low-income students in [location] with school supplies, uniforms, fees, or educational materials through direct payments to approved schools and vendors.

That is clear, fundable, measurable, and manageable.




